The attached image is a Western blot illustrating IL-1β expression and secretion by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs) under various treatment conditions, as part of Figure 7(D). It shows that when BMDCs are primed with LPS and exposed to Nano-11, the active 17 kD form of IL-1β is secreted into the supernatant. In the cell lysate, pro-IL-1β (30 kD) is evident with LPS treatment, which is then processed to the active 17 kD form upon addition of Nano-11. This confirms that Nano-11, a dendrimer-like α-D-glucan nanoparticle, effectively induces the cleavage and secretion of active IL-1β, a key pro-inflammatory cytokine, supporting its role in dendritic cell activation and its utility as a vaccine adjuvant.